                                "example_id": "eec7a46b-2150-4777-a60b-bc1a12c168d7",
                                "sense_id": "0f8a6107-f05f-3c00-bc25-561810909915",
                                "text": "There were slow boys and bashful boys, feeble boys and riotous boys, boys that lisped and boys that stuttered, one or two lame ones, and a merry little quadroon, who could not be taken in elsewhere, but who was welcome to the ‘Bhaer-garten’, though some people predicted that his admission would ruin the school."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1250b10c-6782-4f54-8bb4-917580c13fbb",
                                "sense_id": "0f8a6107-f05f-3c00-bc25-561810909915",
                                "text": "1938, Xavier Herbert, Capricornia, Chapter V, p. 63; Chapter VIII, p. 120 https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb\nDiana was a black quadroon, her father being a blackfellow.\nHe was the father of four quadroons who were regarded as half-castes because the lighter part of their mother's blood was Asiatic, and he was only too well aware of what their future would be should he desert them."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
